--- IMPLEMENTATION NOTES -----------------------------------------------------
* Bound through @Observable SpeedProfilePageModel (P1/S8); SpeedProfileSource seam
  composes web useSpeedProfile (GET /analytics/speed-profile [start,end]) + useDrives.
  No networking in the view (ADR-004). InMemorySpeedProfileSource backs previews+tests.
* Units: SI on the wire; converted ONLY at the display boundary. SpeedProfileUnits
  mirrors web/src/lib/unitConversion.ts (m/s->km/h ×3600/1000, m/s->mph ×3600/1609.344;
  Wh/km->Wh/mi ×1.609344) — pinned by tests. Gauge maxima 55.56 / 69.44 m/s (web).
* getEfficiency parity: energyUsedWh/(distanceM/1000), else battery delta
  (battUsed×0.75×1000/km), else nil. Per-bucket efficiency accumulation + 4-tier scatter
  colours + 3-tier bucket-efficiency colours reproduced (SpeedProfileProjection).
* No hidden panels (ADR-011 / repo rule #6): the scatter panel (web `scatterData>3`
  guard) and the insight panel (web `optimalSpeedMps>0` guard) are ALWAYS rendered with
  an in-panel empty row / fallback message instead of being conditionally removed.
* HIG-native: TSGlassPanel materials (ADR-005), Swift Charts (never WKWebView), Swift
  semantic colour tokens (Color.TS.*) — web literal hexes mapped to tiered tokens; light/
  dark + increased-contrast + Dynamic Type via the generated token ramp; VoiceOver
  labels/values + .isHeader traits; ContentUnavailableView for empty (ADR-014/015).
* Navigation: `.navigationTitle` set; surface is a public, hostable View
  (SpeedProfilePage(model:)) like all peers. /speed-profile is NOT a top-level AppRoute
  case (locked enum, sub-page of driving/analytics), so no new top-level route is added
  (avoids out-of-scope IA drift); hostable via AppRouteHostRegistry at integration time.

